{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01KVNEyBC1ev6pANHemf2Auc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the research context carefully to define three tiers for the Dream simulation.\n\nKey facts from the project:\n- Previous round: all three tiers got 3/6 Weak Reject\n- Target: best ≥ 4/6 Weak Accept, median ≥ 3.5/6 Borderline\n- Core new contribution: temporal label model (replacing vanilla majority vote)\n- New additions: FlyingSquid baseline, outcome_backpropagation sensitivity analysis, expanded related work\n\n\n- Completed experiments show strong probe performance (F1=0.9055-0.9185) with GRU outperforming mean pooling, and full-data results (F1=0.8468) demonstrating noise tolerance. The critical path forward involves running the temporal label model, FlyingSquid baseline, outcome backpropagation sensitivity analysis, and human annotation experiments to validate the core contributions.\n\n- I'm organizing the evaluation around four key questions: whether the temporal label model actually delivers improvements over majority voting, if cross-agent transfer generalizes across different agents, whether human annotation supports the approach, and ultimately whether the narrative is compelling enough for publication. I'm tracking specific metrics like label quality gains, probe performance on the gold set, transfer F1 scores between agents, and cost-accuracy tradeoffs for the LLM-as-judge baseline.\n\nNow I'm defining success tiers based on how convincingly these claims hold up. The best case is when the temporal model clearly outperforms both majority voting and FlyingSquid on the gold set, cross-agent transfer works reliably, the LLM-as-judge comparison looks favorable, and there's no evidence of outcome leakage. The middle tier allows for modest improvements and some transfer degradation as long as it's still useful. The worst case would require reframing if the temporal model doesn't beat FlyingSquid or if transfer fails entirely. I need to establish specific numerical thresholds for each tier to guide the evaluation. Looking at the cross-agent transfer results, the probe doesn't clearly outperform the transferred label functions. For the LLM-as-judge comparison, the probe dominates on the cost-efficiency frontier with much lower computational overhead, though the chain-of-thought variant does achieve better F1 in some cases. On the outcome_bp sensitivity front, holding out that variable keeps performance drops minimal, but larger leakage scenarios show concerning degradation. The inter-annotator agreement on the human gold set ranges from strong to weak depending on the task, and the review scores top out at 4.0.\n\nNow I'm reconsidering the worst-case narrative—the instruction emphasizes staying within the same venue rather than downgrading, so I need to find a different angle that still targets EMNLP. I'm also identifying the core assumptions: that label functions exhibit meaningful temporal dynamics worth exploiting, that the temporal label model substantially improves over majority voting and FlyingSquid, and that the probe trained on these labels outperforms baselines.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12005,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12005},"output_tokens":19,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1e5dc95c-0b0b-4906-b22a-47749c2b2765","uuid":"4f8949ca-866a-42df-90d2-4f509e1c8a6a"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01KVNEyBC1ev6pANHemf2Auc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntiers:\n  best:\n    meaning: \"Temporal label model 构成清晰方法论贡献：在 gold set 上显著优于 MV 和 FlyingSquid，cross-agent 迁移验证 probe 学到通用信号，outcome_bp 泄露可忽略，三条 claims 完全成立\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"A1: LF 时序动态显著且可量化（leading/lagging offset ≥1.5 steps，p<0.01）\"\n      - \"A2: Temporal label model 在 gold set 上标签质量显著优于 MV（+8pp+）且明确优于 FlyingSquid（+4pp+）\"\n      - \"A3: Probe 在 gold set 上超越 LF oracle（student exceeds teacher 成立）\"\n      - \"A4: Cross-agent 迁移 probe 保持有效（F1≥0.75），LF oracle 严重退化（F1 drop ≥15pp）\"\n      - \"A5: Hold-out outcome_bp 后 probe F1 下降 <2pp，泄露可忽略\"\n      - \"A6: Human gold set Fleiss κ≥0.75，标注质量高\"\n      - \"A7: Probe 在 cost-accuracy Pareto 前沿严格优于 LLM-as-judge（含 CoT）\"\n    number_ranges:\n      temporal_lm_vs_mv_gold_f1_gain_pp: [8, 15]\n      temporal_lm_vs_flyingsquid_gold_f1_gain_pp: [4, 10]\n      probe_gold_set_macro_f1: [0.83, 0.89]\n      probe_gold_vs_lf_oracle_gain_pp: [4, 10]\n      cross_agent_probe_macro_f1: [0.75, 0.85]\n      cross_agent_lf_oracle_degradation_pp: [15, 30]\n      outcome_bp_holdout_f1_drop_pp: [0, 2]\n      human_gold_fleiss_kappa: [0.75, 0.90]\n      llm_judge_cot_macro_f1: [0.78, 0.84]\n      probe_vs_llm_judge_f1_gap_pp: [2, 8]\n      probe_cost_speedup_vs_llm: [500, 800]\n      expected_review_score: [4.0, 4.5]\n    narrative_direction: \"原始 framing 完全成立。Temporal label model 作为对 data programming 在序列数据上的方法论贡献立得住——i.i.d. 假设违反问题有实证、有解法、有显著增益。三层贡献（temporal label model → probe exceeds teacher → cross-agent transfer）逻辑链完整。论文直接按 paper_framing 写，claims 无需降级。headline: 'Temporal label model improves label quality by X% over MV; probe trained on these labels achieves Y F1, outperforming LF oracle and LLM-as-judge while being 600× faster.'\"\n\n  median:\n    meaning: \"Temporal label model 有效但优势有限：优于 MV 但仅 marginally 优于 FlyingSquid，cross-agent 迁移有退化但仍 positive，outcome_bp 有一定泄露需加 caveat。需调整 claim 强度，补充消融支撑\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"A1: LF 时序动态存在但 effect size 中等（offset 显著但 temporal LM 的增益主要来自少数 LF 对）\"\n      - \"A2: Temporal label model 优于 MV（+4pp+）但 vs FlyingSquid 仅 marginal（+1~3pp，部分 metric 不显著）\"\n      - \"A3: Probe 在 gold set 上与 LF oracle 持平或略优（+1~3pp），student-exceeds-teacher 效应弱\"\n      - \"A4: Cross-agent 迁移 probe 有退化但仍可用（F1=0.65-0.75），LF oracle 退化更严重\"\n      - \"A5: Hold-out outcome_bp 后 F1 下降 3-5pp，可控但需讨论\"\n      - \"A6: Human gold set Fleiss κ=0.60-0.75，可接受但 borderline\"\n      - \"A7: Probe F1 与 LLM-as-judge CoT 持平或略低，但成本优势仍显著\"\n    number_ranges:\n      temporal_lm_vs_mv_gold_f1_gain_pp: [4, 8]\n      temporal_lm_vs_flyingsquid_gold_f1_gain_pp: [1, 4]\n      probe_gold_set_macro_f1: [0.76, 0.83]\n      probe_gold_vs_lf_oracle_gain_pp: [1, 4]\n      cross_agent_probe_macro_f1: [0.65, 0.75]\n      cross_agent_lf_oracle_degradation_pp: [8, 18]\n      outcome_bp_holdout_f1_drop_pp: [3, 5]\n      human_gold_fleiss_kappa: [0.60, 0.75]\n      llm_judge_cot_macro_f1: [0.80, 0.86]\n      probe_vs_llm_judge_f1_gap_pp: [-3, 2]\n      probe_cost_speedup_vs_llm: [500, 800]\n      expected_review_score: [3.5, 4.0]\n    narrative_direction: \"Claim 1 降级：temporal label model 从 '方法论贡献' 调整为 'temporal-aware aggregation that consistently improves over naive MV and performs comparably to learned label models while being interpretable'。强调 temporal LM 的优势不在绝对 F1 差异，而在可解释性（每个 LF 的 temporal role 可 inspect）和不需要 LF 条件独立性假设。Claim 2 保持但弱化 student-exceeds-teacher 表述为 'probe matches or exceeds heuristic baselines without access to LFs at inference'。Claim 3 保持但加 degradation caveat。补充 ablation 实验（encoder ablation、window size）增加 empirical depth 弥补 novelty 不足。论文叙事重心从 'temporal label model 是核心方法论贡献' 偏移到 'systematic weak supervision pipeline for agent progress estimation with temporal insights'。\"\n\n  worst:\n    meaning: \"Temporal label model 无法显著超越 FlyingSquid（甚至持平/略低），核心方法论贡献不成立；outcome_bp 泄露严重动摇标签可靠性；cross-agent 迁移效果差。需要彻底 reframe 但仍冲 EMNLP\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"A1: LF 时序动态存在但 temporal label model 无法将其转化为标签质量增益（FlyingSquid 的相关性建模已够用）\"\n      - \"A2: Temporal label model vs FlyingSquid 无显著差异甚至更差（-2~+1pp）\"\n      - \"A3: Probe 在 gold set 上低于或持平 LF oracle，student-exceeds-teacher 不成立\"\n      - \"A4: Cross-agent 迁移 probe 退化严重（F1<0.65），迁移 claim 不成立\"\n      - \"A5: Hold-out outcome_bp 后 F1 下降 >5pp，泄露问题实质性\"\n      - \"A6: Human gold set Fleiss κ<0.60，stagnation 边界模糊\"\n      - \"A7: LLM-as-judge CoT 在 F1 上明确优于 probe\"\n    number_ranges:\n      temporal_lm_vs_mv_gold_f1_gain_pp: [1, 4]\n      temporal_lm_vs_flyingsquid_gold_f1_gain_pp: [-2, 1]\n      probe_gold_set_macro_f1: [0.68, 0.76]\n      probe_gold_vs_lf_oracle_gain_pp: [-3, 1]\n      cross_agent_probe_macro_f1: [0.55, 0.65]\n      cross_agent_lf_oracle_degradation_pp: [3, 10]\n      outcome_bp_holdout_f1_drop_pp: [5, 12]\n      human_gold_fleiss_kappa: [0.45, 0.60]\n      llm_judge_cot_macro_f1: [0.82, 0.88]\n      probe_vs_llm_judge_f1_gap_pp: [-8, -3]\n      probe_cost_speedup_vs_llm: [500, 800]\n      expected_review_score: [3.0, 3.5]\n    narrative_direction: \"核心假设（temporal label model 作为方法论贡献）不成立，需 reframe。新 angle：将论文从 'temporal label model 方法贡献' 转向 'empirical study on weak supervision for agent behavior understanding'——贡献变为：(1) 系统性揭示标准 data programming 在 agent trajectory 上的 failure modes（i.i.d. 违反的实证分析、LF temporal dynamics 的 characterization、outcome_bp 泄露的量化），这本身是对 WS community 的实证贡献；(2) 提出 stagnation taxonomy 和 window-level formulation 作为 agent monitoring 的新任务定义（task contribution）；(3) 实证发现 probe 在高噪声标签上的鲁棒性（conf≥1 vs conf≥2 的 gap 分析）和 GRU 时序建模的增量价值（+12.7pp vs mean-pool on noisy labels）。成本优势仍可讲（600× faster than LLM），但降为 practical advantage 而非 main claim。论文改为 Findings of EMNLP 风格的实证研究，篇幅不变但 claim 从 method contribution 转为 task+analysis contribution。仍投 EMNLP ARR May cycle——Findings track 接受 solid empirical work with useful negative results。\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12005,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12005},"output_tokens":19,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1e5dc95c-0b0b-4906-b22a-47749c2b2765","uuid":"095f3120-197c-4a5c-9d99-17c963b69a23"}
